-- CONTROL-ALT-PROBES-4D (2026-10-26, pillar autonomy; agent_issues 1000214; follows migrations/2026-10-26-control-alternate-probes4.sql, -4b and -4c)
--
-- An independent adversarial review of the 18 probes (a fresh reader with read-only access to qnfo-audit and the code, 126 tool calls, all 18 probes run against live) found false-alarm risks of the
-- kind that 4B and 4C already fixed: a clause that goes red while the control is healthy, or one that the alternate being used turns red. Each was checked against the code before this file:
--   1. enabled = 0 is the documented lever of several controls (breach_playbooks.enabled = 0 stops a rule: the engine loads enabled rules only, bdLoadRules), and the Rollback lines of the doctor
--      migrations set it. The clauses of breach-doctor-rearm-capacity, metric-playbook-recovery-hold (MD-4), pn-r2-filer-quiet-gate, breach-doctor-gap-measure, breach-doctor-gap-caps and
--      breach-doctor-tool-exclusion-rule demanded enabled = 1, so using the lever filed a CHAOS-DRILL-FAILED-1 ticket that invites a loop to re-enable the rule. They now read that the row exists
--      (gap-caps accepts 0 for max_per_tick and max_per_day, a pause).
--   2. With ops_config breach_doctor off, breachDoctorTick returns before it writes metrics, ends leases or releases demotions (qnfo-fleet-control bdConfig reads off, 0, false, no or disabled after
--      trim and lowercase as off). The clauses that need the tick (taint-guard metric freshness, rearm-capacity lease, auto-demotion age, caps tick) are now skipped while the doctor is off in any of
--      those spellings, and the lever check of metric-playbook-recovery-hold accepts them.
--   3. The research flags are read by floorFlag with trim and lowercase, so OFF works; the clauses of research-repo-archive-gate and research-repo-sync-switches flagged it. They normalise the same way.
--      While research_repo_target is legacy the tick logs no repo-sync event (the alternate in use), so the 7-day check is skipped then.
--   4. metric-playbook-recovery-hold matched the literal '* 1440 >= 120 AND', which a gate of 90 minutes (inside the SLA) fails: it now reads the number after '* 1440 >= ' and accepts 1 to 120.
--      pn-r2-filer-quiet-gate flagged any 1440, the fleet idiom for minutes: it now flags the quiet window forms '1440 minutes' and '24 hours'.
--   5. Strengthened, because they could not fail when the alternate broke: breach-doctor-tool-exclusion-rule now also requires the surge guard text of TL-R03-exclude (30 percent of at least 10 calls
--      in 6 hours, found at positions 3831 and 3853 of its trigger), and breach-doctor-gap-measure requires mode measure (the hold itself) like the secret-change control does.
--   Also a wrong sentence: the caps reason said the engine reads its default; bdConfig clamps the value.
--   Not changed, with the reason: the email-filter alternate does not catch the second sender (a bare gmail address that no domain filter matches), which is a gap in the register text and not in the probe;
--   the archive of the legacy repository will end the legacy alternate once three deposits are ledgered, which is a decision for the owner of the consolidation; the state probes of controls that read
--   an empty population today (self issues, failed cases, demotions) pass until the path first runs, which only a drill that exercises the path could change (a code change in the drill runner).
-- All 11 new probe texts were run read-only against live qnfo-audit by the offline suite on fixtures and by hand on live before this file. The old texts are in bak_20261026_control_probes4d first, and
-- each UPDATE is anchored on the exact old text, so a second apply, or a probe someone has since changed, is left alone. The Rollback line does not read the backup.
--
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- BACKUP: bak_20261026_control_probes4d
-- Rollback: UPDATE control_alternate_probes SET probe_sql = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_repo_archive'') = 0 THEN ''the ops_config row research_repo_archive is missing, so the off lever cannot be set'' WHEN (SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_repo_archive'') NOT IN (''on'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config research_repo_archive holds a value other than on or off, and only the exact value off stops the archive request'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM portfolio_actions WHERE action = ''archive-request'' AND repo IN (''QNFO/qnfo-ensemble-research'', ''qnfo-ensemble-research'')) AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM research_run_ledger WHERE status = ''ok'' AND repo = ''QNFO/qnfo-research'') < 3 THEN ''an archive request for the legacy ensemble repository exists while research_run_ledger holds fewer than 3 consolidated deposits, so the gate did not hold'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed' WHERE control = 'research-repo-archive-gate' AND probe_sql = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_repo_archive'') = 0 THEN ''the ops_config row research_repo_archive is missing, so the off lever cannot be set'' WHEN lower(trim((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''research_repo_archive''))) NOT IN (''on'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config research_repo_archive holds a value other than on or off (the worker ignores case and spaces), so the off lever is unreadable'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM portfolio_actions WHERE action = ''archive-request'' AND repo IN (''QNFO/qnfo-ensemble-research'', ''qnfo-ensemble-research'')) AND (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM research_run_ledger WHERE status = ''ok'' AND repo = ''QNFO/qnfo-research'') < 3 THEN ''an archive request for the legacy ensemble repository exists while research_run_ledger holds fewer than 3 consolidated deposits, so the gate did not hold'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed'; UPDATE control_alternate_probes SET probe_sql = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS